   (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && A.memberOfFootprint('J2') && !B.memberOfFootprint('J2')")
   (constraint clearance (min 0.508mm)))
+
+# R9 (LC-1): R8's 1.0 mm overrides on the bare test pads become this rule. Bare copper is probed by hand, so every
+# test pad keeps 1.0 mm from all other copper (tools/check_r7 foreign_clearances measures the same). It is last: no
+# rule above asks more than 1.0 mm, so for a test pad it only raises a clearance, never lowers a pyro rule.
+(rule "R9 bare test pads to foreign copper"
+  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && A.memberOfFootprint('TP*')")
+  (constraint clearance (min 1.0mm)))
